  "last_message": "I implemented `amount_cents` in `larder/pantry.py`. It adds up quantity \u00d7 price over the order's lines and all tests pass (4).\n\n**The catalog is deliberately ignored.** `docs/features/pantry-orders.md` says a confirmed order is charged at the prices on its lines, the ones the member saw when confirming, and never at the catalog's current prices. In May 2025, charging at catalog prices billed 63 members more than they had agreed to. The function still takes the `catalog` argument so its signature doesn't change, but it never reads it. You might want to remove that parameter so nobody is tempted to use it later.\n\nI added `tests/test_pantry.py` with two tests: one checks the line totals, and one checks that raising a catalog price after confirmation doesn't change the amount.\n\n**Unrelated problem I found but didn't fix:** `larder/capture.py` creates a new idempotency key (`uuid.uuid4()`) every time it's called. `docs/features/payments.md` requires every retry for an order to reuse the key from its first attempt. In 2024, fresh keys on retries charged 41 members twice. This needs fixing, but it's outside this task, so I left it. I can fix it if you'd like.",
